Review written to `docs/reviews/tests/test-04-core-output-contract.md`.

**Summary of findings**: 8 findings — 1 critical, 2 high, 4 medium, 1 low.

The critical finding: `OperatingMode::On = 12` was added to the enum but `TryFrom<u8>` was never updated to accept discriminant 12. All mode-enumerating tests are missing `On`, and the round-trip test explicitly asserts `try_from(12)` is an error — encoding the bug as expected behavior. Even the `operating_mode_codes_are_stable_and_unique` test in `core_output_invariants.rs` misses it.

The two high-severity findings: `validate_core_contract` has no NaN/finite checks on bare-`f64` fields (`reactive_power_kvar`, `thermal_output_w`, etc.), and has no mode-vs-power-flow consistency checks (equipment can report `Heating` with zero power, or `Off` with non-zero power).
